Track 1: The Timetable Swallows Itself
- Story & Context: Mateo Ruzic had barely settled into compartment 4 of the Munich-to-Zagreb Nightjet when the emergency brakes seized outside Salzburg, filling the corridor with the bitter reek of scorched iron brake pads and stale espresso. Instead of bracing for impact, he jammed a silent brass practice mute into his BBb tuba, matching the pneumatic wheeze of the undercarriage with guttural, syncopated dembow chugs. Three bleary-eyed passengers staggered into the aisle holding battery-powered drum modules, locking their flickering screens to the locomotive’s violent lurch while a furious conductor shouted "The rails don't negotiate, they just drop" before abandoning his manifest to dance. By the time the hydraulic line bled out, the compartment floor had become the epicenter of a new sonic movement.
