Track 2: Are You Sleeping Through the Junction?
- Story & Context: Inés Alarcón spent three consecutive winters riding the 01:14 sleeper shuttle through Linz Hauptbahnhof, running solely on cheap nicotine and the freezing condensation trickling off the double-glazed passenger windows. Her entire existence lived inside a battered pocket synth and an auxiliary ribbon mic taped to the train’s exhaust vent, capturing the low rumble she needed to ground her confession. When a conductor threatened to throw her off into the sub-zero slush for playing past curfew, she looked him in the eye and whispered "Tell the conductor I traded my ticket for forty pounds of brass," cranking the sousaphone sub-bass until the carriage windows rattled in their rubber gaskets. She never reached her destination, choosing instead to loop the same five minor chords across four international borders.
